## Summary

Implemented **`page:trips/TripDetail`** as a native SwiftUI / Apple HIG screen at full web parity, adaptive across macOS + iOS — `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Trips/` (7 files, 758 lines).

**Architecture (mirrors shipped sibling pages):**
- `TripDetailPageModel` — `@MainActor @Observable`, single source of truth driving all four data states; no networking in the view (ADR-004).
- `TripDetailDataSource` seam keeps the web hook name `useTrip` (← `GET /trips/{id}`); Sample/Empty/Failing doubles exercise success/empty/error.
- SI converts **only** at the render boundary via the shared `Units` facade (ADR-005) — Energy pinned to raw Wh, Cost to currency, exactly as the web does.

**Parity — `PARITY_COVERED=21/21`:** 5 panels (Distance, Energy-Used, Efficiency, Cost, GlassPanel5 KVList) · 4 states (loading skeleton, empty/notFound, error+retry, success) · 12 strings (all resolve from `Localizable.xcstrings` via the catalog's `translation.trips.detail.*` entries, web key names preserved).

